            <ArticleTitle>[Diet and the heart: end of an era? or beginning of a hope?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>683-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A critical review is made of a recent article by G. Mann (New Engl. J. Med., 297, 644, 1977) where an attack is moved to the theory according which the diet is a basic factor in the epidemic of coronary heart disease. Most of the Mann' arguments are contradicted and an attempt is made to explain why his article has received such a large attention also outisde the strictly scientific mass-media.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
